1
00:00:04,293 --> 00:00:13,513
Collect intake and consent before arrival — Patients ▸ Patient Intake — Get the paperwork done before the patient walks in, not in the waiting room.

2
00:00:19,009 --> 00:00:24,794
Patients ▸ Patient Intake tracks the paperwork you asked for and whether it came back.

3
00:00:24,794 --> 00:00:30,737
The three tabs are three different things, and mixing them up is the usual confusion.

4
00:00:30,737 --> 00:00:42,622
Intake forms are single questionnaires sent to one patient, each with its own status: sent, in progress, completed.

5
00:00:42,622 --> 00:00:54,197
Intake flows are packets — several forms sent as one journey, so a new patient gets everything in a single link.

6
00:00:54,197 --> 00:01:05,291
Consent forms are the signed ones. They record who signed, when, and how — and they carry an expiry.

7
00:01:05,291 --> 00:01:12,291
Completed answers land on the chart, so the clinician reads them before the visit rather than during it.

8
00:01:12,291 --> 00:01:17,275
And a consent signed at home is one less clipboard in the waiting room.

9
00:01:18,846 --> 00:01:31,536
What you just did

10
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:41,220
